local ADDON_NAME, ns = ...

-- The Burning Crusade talent trees, whole: every talent in every tree, where
-- it sits, how many ranks it has and which talent it needs first.
--
-- Generated from the game's own Talent and TalentTab tables for the
-- wow_anniversary client, as exported by wago.tools -- the same data the
-- in-game talent frame and Wowhead's calculator are drawn from -- by
-- arenaplus.live/tools/build_tbc_talents.py. Do not edit by hand.
--
-- A Mists client cannot ask for these: GetTalentInfo only ever describes the
-- player's own class on the client they are playing. Shipping them is what
-- lets an Anniversary rogue's build be drawn as a tree from any client.
--
--   [class] = { { name, background, icon, talents = {
--       { row, column, { rank spell ids }, requires, icon, name }, ... } }, ... }
--
-- row and column count from zero, as the game stores them. requires is the
-- index, within the same tree, of the talent that must be taken first.
-- icon is a file id, which SetTexture takes as it is. The name ships because a
-- Mists client asked about a TBC rank spell answers nothing.

